s cochlear sensory cells from acoustic trauma in the guinea-pig</article-title><source><italic>Neuroscience</italic></source><year>2002</year><volume>111</volume><issue>3</issue><fpage>635</fpage><lpage>648</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">12031350</pub-id></element-citation></ref><ref id="B20"><label>20</label><element-citation publication-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Cazals</surname><given-names>Y</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Auditory sensori-neural alterations induced by salicylate</article-title><source><italic>Progress in Neurobiology</italic></source><year>2000</year><volume>62</volume><issue>6</issue><fpage>583</fpage><lpage>631</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">10880852</pub-id></element-citation></ref><ref id="B23"><label>21</label><element-citation publication-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Heffner</surname><given-names>HE</given-names></name><name><surname>Harrington</surname><given-names>IA</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Tinnitus in hamsters following exposure to intense sound</article-title><source><italic>Hearing Research</italic></source><year>2002</year><volume>170</volume><issue>1-2</issue><fpage>83</fpage><lpage>95</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">12208543</pub-id></element-citation></ref><ref id="B21"><label>22</label><element-citation publication-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Cahani</surname><given-names>M</given-names></name><name><surname>Paul</surname><given-names>G</given-names></name><name><surname>Shahar</surname><given-names>A</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Tinnitus pitch and acoustic trauma</article-title><source><italic>Audiology</italic></source><year>1983</year><volume>22</volume><issue>4</issue><fpage>357</fpage><lpage>363</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">6615340</pub-id></element-citation></ref><ref id="B22"><label>23</label><element-citation publicati